{
  "id": "patterns-relationships-and-graphs",
  "title": "Patterns, Relationships and Graphs",
  "term": 1,
  "summary": "Representing relationships with words, tables, formulas and graphs; dependent and independent variables; direct and inverse proportion; and reading points of intersection.",
  "notes": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variables"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "The **independent variable** is the one you choose or control (e.g. number of kilometres travelled). It goes on the **horizontal** axis.",
        "The **dependent variable** depends on it (e.g. cost of the trip). It goes on the **vertical** axis."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Four ways to show a relationship"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 1: a taxi company",
      "problem": "A shuttle service charges R50 plus R12 per kilometre. Show the relationship in words, as a formula, as a table and as a graph.",
      "steps": [
        "Words: cost = R50 + R12 for every kilometre.",
        "Formula: $C = 50 + 12d$, where $d$ is the distance in km.",
        "Table: $d$ = 0; 5; 10; 15; 20 gives $C$ = R50; R110; R170; R230; R290."
      ],
      "answer": "A straight-line (linear) graph starting at R50"
    },
