      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 2: inverse proportion",
      "problem": "4 builders take 15 days to build a wall. How long would 6 builders take, working at the same rate?",
      "steps": [
        "Total work = 4 × 15 = 60 builder-days.",
        "6 builders: 60 ÷ 6 = 10 days"
      ],
      "answer": "10 days"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing options"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "When two graphs are drawn on the same axes, the **point of intersection** shows where both options cost the same (the **break-even point**). Before it, the lower graph is cheaper; after it, the other graph is cheaper."
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 3",
      "problem": "Using the graph: a normal taxi charges R18 per km with no fixed fee. For which distances is the shuttle cheaper?",
      "steps": [
